<!--{ an00 : formula | hidden }-->
<% texl.import "~/lib/stilo/index.texl" ~> (lib -> bind "stilo" lib.data.stilo) %>
<!--{ an01 : markdown }-->
# Calculation note

Mezzanine floor beam — document MZ-003, revision B. The checks of the
[design report](beam-check.texl), with the design data of the
[basis of design](basis-of-design.texl).
<% texl.import "basis-of-design.texl" ~> (d -> bind "bod" d.data) %>
<!--{ an02 : formula | hidden }-->
<%
# Rounds x to n decimals.
fix = (x, n) -> math.round (x * 10 ^ n) / 10 ^ n,

# A ratio as a whole percentage.
pct = x -> math.round (x * 100),

# The checks of one section, with the data of the basis of design. Loads in
# kN/m (= N/mm), lengths in mm for the stresses and deflections.
check = s -> (
    L = bod.L * 1000,
    gs = s.mass * 9.81 / 1000,
    g = bod.gk + gs,
    q = bod.qk,
    qd = bod.gammaG * g + bod.gammaQ * q,
    MEd = qd * bod.L ^ 2 / 8,
    VEd = qd * bod.L / 2,
    sigma = MEd * 10 ^ 6 / s.W,
    fyd = bod.fy / bod.gammaM0,
    VRd = s.Av * bod.fy / ((math.sqrt 3) * bod.gammaM0) / 1000,
    d = 5 * (g + q) * L ^ 4 / (384 * bod.E * s.I),
    dq = 5 * q * L ^ 4 / (384 * bod.E * s.I),
    d_lim = L / bod.deflection_total,
    dq_lim = L / bod.deflection_variable,
    u_M = sigma / fyd,
    u_V = VEd / VRd,
    u_d = d / d_lim,
    u_dq = dq / dq_lim,
    u = math.max (u_M, u_V, u_d, u_dq),
    governing = (u == u_M) ? "bending" ; ((u == u_V) ? "shear" ;
        ((u == u_d) ? "total deflection" ; "deflection under variable load")),
    {
        section: s, gs: gs, g: g, q: q, qd: qd, MEd: MEd, VEd: VEd,
        sigma: sigma, fyd: fyd, VRd: VRd, d: d, dq: dq,
        d_lim: d_lim, dq_lim: dq_lim,
        u_M: u_M, u_V: u_V, u_d: u_d, u_dq: u_dq, u: u,
        governing: governing, ok: u <= 1
    }
)
%>
<!--{ an03 : markdown }-->
## 1 Method

The beam is simply supported and carries a uniform load, so the midspan
moment, the end shear and the midspan deflection are

$$
M_{Ed} = \frac{q_d L^2}{8}, \qquad V_{Ed} = \frac{q_d L}{2}, \qquad
\delta = \frac{5\,q\,L^4}{384\,E\,I}
$$

The bending check is elastic, $\sigma = M_{Ed} / W \le f_y / \gamma_{M0}$,
which is conservative for an IPE section. The shear resistance is
$V_{Rd} = A_v f_y / (\sqrt{3}\,\gamma_{M0})$ (EN 1993-1-1, 6.2.6). The
deck restrains the compression flange, so lateral-torsional buckling is
not checked (basis of design, section 2). The self-weight of the beam is
added to the permanent load.
<!--{ an04 : markdown }-->
## 2 Proposed section

<% r = check bod.section %>
The <% r.section.name %> weighs <% r.section.mass %> kg/m, a self-weight
$g_s = <% fix (r.gs, 2) %>\ \text{kN/m}$. The line loads on the beam in each
combination are:
<!--{ an05 : markdown }-->
<% combinations = stilo.dataframe {
    columns: ["Combination", "γG", "γQ", "q (kN/m)"],
    rows: [(list.enum bod.combinations.rows) => (c -> [c 0, c 1, c 2, fix (c 1 * r.g + c 2 * r.q, 2)])]
} %>
<% combinations %>
<caption>Table 1: Line loads on the <% r.section.name %>, self-weight included.</caption>
<!--{ an06 : markdown }-->
### 2.1 Strength

$$
q_d = \gamma_G\,(g_k + g_s) + \gamma_Q\,q_k = <% fix (r.qd, 2) %>\ \text{kN/m}
$$

$$
M_{Ed} = <% fix (r.MEd, 1) %>\ \text{kNm}, \qquad
\sigma = \frac{M_{Ed}}{W} = <% math.round r.sigma %>\ \text{N/mm}^2, \qquad
f_{yd} = \frac{f_y}{\gamma_{M0}} = <% math.round r.fyd %>\ \text{N/mm}^2
$$

$$
V_{Ed} = <% fix (r.VEd, 1) %>\ \text{kN}, \qquad
V_{Rd} = \frac{A_v f_y}{\sqrt{3}\,\gamma_{M0}} = <% fix (r.VRd, 1) %>\ \text{kN}
$$
<!--{ an07 : markdown }-->
### 2.2 Deflection

Under the characteristic combination, the total deflection and the
deflection under the variable load alone are

$$
\delta = <% fix (r.d, 1) %>\ \text{mm} \le \frac{L}{<% bod.deflection_total %>} = <% fix (r.d_lim, 1) %>\ \text{mm},
\qquad
\delta_q = <% fix (r.dq, 1) %>\ \text{mm} \le \frac{L}{<% bod.deflection_variable %>} = <% fix (r.dq_lim, 1) %>\ \text{mm}
$$
<!--{ an08 : markdown }-->
### 2.3 Summary

| Check | Effect | Limit | Utilisation |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Bending | <% math.round r.sigma %> N/mm² | <% math.round r.fyd %> N/mm² | <% pct r.u_M %> % |
| Shear | <% fix (r.VEd, 1) %> kN | <% fix (r.VRd, 1) %> kN | <% pct r.u_V %> % |
| Total deflection | <% fix (r.d, 1) %> mm | <% fix (r.d_lim, 1) %> mm | <% pct r.u_d %> % |
| Deflection, variable load | <% fix (r.dq, 1) %> mm | <% fix (r.dq_lim, 1) %> mm | <% pct r.u_dq %> % |
<caption>Table 2: Checks of the <% r.section.name %>.</caption>

The <% r.section.name %> is <% r.ok ? "**adequate**" ; "**not adequate**" %>:
the governing check is <% r.governing %>, at <% pct r.u %> %.
<!--[ Marco: fine for the report. ]-->
<!--{ an09 : markdown }-->
## 3 Alternative sections

The same checks for the IPE sections of the steel library, lightest first.

<%
results = [(list.enum [
    bod.steel.IPE.IPE240, bod.steel.IPE.IPE270,
    bod.steel.IPE.IPE300, bod.steel.IPE.IPE330
]) => check],
alternatives = stilo.dataframe {
    columns: ["Section", "Mass (kg/m)", "Bending (%)", "Shear (%)", "δ (%)", "δq (%)", "Result"],
    rows: [(list.enum results) => (a -> [
        a.section.name, a.section.mass, pct a.u_M, pct a.u_V, pct a.u_d, pct a.u_dq,
        (a.ok ? "adequate" ; "not adequate")
    ])]
},
lightest = [(list.enum results) => (a -> a.ok ? a)] 0
%>
<% alternatives %>
<caption>Table 3: Utilisation of the IPE sections, by check; δ is the total deflection,
δq the deflection under variable load.</caption>

The lightest adequate section is the <% lightest.section.name %>, governed by
<% lightest.governing %> at <% pct lightest.u %> %.
<!--[ Anna: try an IPE 270 too. ]-->
<!--[ Marco: done, see table 3. ]-->
